# Docker image only runs `./gradlew executableJar -x test` (see Dockerfile).
# Keep the build context limited to sources + Gradle wrapper — not tests, docs, or VCS history.
# BUILD_REVISION is passed as a build-arg from CI (no .git needed in context).

# --- Version control & CI ---
.git
.github

# --- Gradle outputs & caches (created by the test step before docker build on CI) ---
.gradle
build
out
tmp
.nb-gradle

# --- IDE / editor ---
.idea
**/.idea
*.iml
**/.classpath
**/.project
**/.settings
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/*.*proj.user
**/*.dbmdl
**/*.jfm

# --- Tests & fixtures (skipped in Docker) ---
src/test
fixtures

# --- Not required to compile the executable jar ---
scripts
integrations
design
distribution
docs
stats
logs

# --- Docs / meta (not used at compile time) ---
LICENSE
README.md
AGENTS.md
**/*.md
!gradle/**/*.md

# --- Secrets / local agent files ---
**/.env
.agent
.secrets
gha-creds-*.json
**/secrets.dev.yaml
**/values.dev.yaml

# --- Container / compose (not part of the Gradle build) ---
**/.dockerignore
**/docker-compose*
**/Dockerfile*
**/azds.yaml
**/charts

# --- Misc build artifacts ---
**/bin
**/obj
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log
**/*.log
**/*.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
